From fd1658a712dbef04799b7169dc18e93afb2dfbe5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:36:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 359/365] DOS-PORT: patch 0359 -- script VM slice 1: decode
 every script once at load (inert unless DOSAGS_VM asks)

MMD is logic-bound on the 486: legacy ccInstance::Run() re-decodes every instruction (argument
fetch, per-argument fixup switch, sccmd_info lookups) on every execution, and that was most of
MMD's 20.5 ms/tick of script VM time (VMPROF, PLAN-FPS lever V). This patch is the first, inert
slice of the replacement (docs/lab/VM-DESIGN.md 2.2-2.3): at the end of ResolveImportFixups each
primary instance's code is decoded ONCE into an index-parallel stream on its ResolvedScriptData
(dcode: the resolved operand words, dstart: a bit per instruction start), with the legacy fixup
semantics applied at load. New file Engine/script/cc_instance_vm.cpp; DJGPP only.

DOSAGS_VM selects, read once: unset/legacy = nothing is decoded (this patch changes nothing);
decode = decode and log one "DOS-PORT vmdecode" line per script; check = also re-derive every
decoded instruction independently and log mismatches. "DOSAGS_VM" joins the RUNMANIFEST env
allowlist. Freed streams are counted ("vmfree" lines).

Lab (docs/lab/VM-SLICE1.md): check mode 0 mismatches over 99k instructions on MMD character select,
AGS Quest (incl. restore) and 5 Days room 3; MMD decodes in ~0.17 s for ~0.54 MB; aq-journeys unchanged.

